#!/bin/sh
# autoharn pre-commit — the mechanical refusals, invoked by REPO-RELATIVE path.
#
# Adapted from claude_harness/tools/hooks/pre-commit [C18]: the old hook reached
# into a sibling repo by absolute path (the two-repo coupling the fresh home must
# not inherit) and ran the ADR-0016 standing-service umbrella gate — which has NO
# services to gate here (the NLP lane stays in the attic, C14). Running it here
# would be a silent vacuous pass (F49). It is therefore NOT wired; it rejoins
# autoharn only when autoharn's first standing service does.
#
# FINAL WIRING (BUILD-BRIEF Step 9, extended 2026-07-11 doc-legibility-indictment commission,
# further extended 2026-07-11 run-10-closure-audit commission, further extended 2026-07-12
# configuration-surface-survey commission, further extended 2026-07-21 setup-TUI field-strategy
# commission Track 1 item 2 — max_lines added, blocking, mechanically alongside fixture_census
# since its own idiom (a same-shaped pipe-and-echo-and-exit-1 block) made the addition mechanical;
# the sibling setup_tui purity-gate wiring queued at ledger row 1847: DISCHARGED 2026-07-22 in the
# session-boundary batch, unrelated to whether THIS gate's wiring was mechanical;
# further extended 2026-07-25 gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness census, ledger row 1234: every
# CONTENT-checking gate below now reads its subject's STAGED bytes by default, not the working
# tree, via the shared gates/_staged_read.py primitive gates/deep_walk_recursion_guard.py's own
# 2026-07-23 fix was extracted into -- see each gate's own inline comment below for its read-mode
# disposition (converted / already-staged / genuinely-tree-correct census / named residual));
# amended 2026-07-26, a fix round on a fresh-context strengthened-tier review of that census's own
# fix (four findings, none of which changed WHICH gates block or on what: (1) the GIT_DIR-inside-
# a-worktree mechanism gates/_staged_read.py's own docstring names as the REAL BUG this census
# closed now has an executable regression case, not just narrative, in seen-red/gates-staged-vs-
# tree-blindness/run_fixtures.py; (2) gates/link_integrity.py's target-existence check now also
# treats a target STAGED FOR DELETION (`git rm --cached`, file still on disk) as not-existing --
# see that gate's own inline comment below; (3) gates/doc_shapes.py's and
# gates/doc_attestation_presence.py's REPORT modes (whole-repo sweeps, never invoked from this
# hook -- see each gate's own inline comment below) now genuinely read the tree unconditionally,
# matching what this file already (correctly) described them as doing; (4) the six converted
# gates' own `git ls-files`/`submodule status`/`diff --cached` ENUMERATION calls (finding which
# files to check, distinct from reading a checked file's bytes) now route through the same
# stripped-env `_staged_read.run_git` the staged-blob read already used, closing the same
# GIT_DIR-inheritance fragility class for those calls too. THIS FILE'S OWN CONTENT is part of
# this fix round (comment corrections only, no gate added/removed/reordered) -- per this
# project's hooks/ discipline, the ACTUAL MERGE of this change into the live hooks/pre-commit a
# running session enforces stays gated for the maintainer's own session-boundary batch, same as
# every other hooks/ edit; this worktree's copy is the reviewable artifact, not a live wire.):
# staging_guard -> no_lazy_imports -> fixture_census -> deep_walk_recursion_guard -> max_lines ->
# link_integrity ->
# apparatus_unknown_keys (gated only when bootstrap/templates/apparatus.json is touched) ->
# doc_shapes -> doc-attestation-presence -> layout_census -> doc-legibility. layout_census is DISABLED here
# as of the maintainer ruling below (2026-07-09); it still appears in this history note as the
# Step-9 design.
# doc-legibility is wired REPORT-ONLY (runs and prints,
# does not block): the C15 scope-widening to ALL tracked *.md surfaces ~1429 acronym reports
# over the migrated corpus — mostly the crude heuristic misfiring on all-caps emphasis words
# and standards acronyms in docs never written against it. Making it a BLOCKING gate over the
# full corpus needs a corpus acronym-sweep (filed, BACKLOG); wiring it blocking now would make
# the repo uncommittable — the maintainer-flagged tension (C15 widen vs Step-9 block vs Step-10
# green). Its seen-red both-polarity proof already exists; only its pre-commit disposition is
# report-only pending the sweep. link_integrity (2026-07-11) checks a DIFFERENT, cheaper
# invariant than doc-legibility (link resolution, not acronym definition) and runs clean over
# the full tracked-*.md corpus today (two principled, documented exclusions — see its own
# docstring) — it BLOCKS. doc_shapes (design/ADR-DRAFT-documentation-discipline.md Rule 3) was
# built, seen-red, and registered days before this wiring but never actually invoked from here
# until now (a gap this same commission's hazard-flagging duty caught and closed alongside its
# own assigned task, not routed around). doc-attestation-presence (ADR-0017, ratified
# 2026-07-11) is authored ENFORCE with no observe/off mode — its own module docstring carries
# the exact WIRING STANZA applied verbatim below, deferred at authoring time only because a
# governed session was live and hooks/ may not be touched while one runs; none is live now. The
# other five non-disabled gates BLOCK too.
#
# Install (once per clone; .git/hooks is unversioned): git config core.hooksPath hooks
set -u
REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
PY="$HOME/w/vdc/venvs/generic/bin/python"
[ -x "$PY" ] || PY="$(command -v python3)"

# staging_guard FIRST — a swept-in path is a scope defect to resolve before any
# content gate matters (finding 33 foreclosure). Repo-local, its one home (P1).
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): this gate reads the staged PATH
# SET (`git diff --cached --name-only`) and per-path blob HASHES via git's own `:path`/`HEAD:path`
# spec -- it never reads a working-tree file's bytes at all. Correctly staged/index-based
# already; no conversion needed.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/staging_guard.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: staging guard FAILED — commit refused (finding 33, commit-scope-sweep)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# no_conflict_markers EARLY — an unresolved merge in the staged additions makes every
# later content gate's verdict meaningless (witnessed: merge b25272f landed raw markers
# in BACKLOG.md past the whole chain; gate added 2026-07-12, same day, seen-red both
# polarities).
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): reads `git diff --cached -U0` --
# the staged diff's own ADDED lines -- already staged-bytes based; no conversion needed.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/no_conflict_markers.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: conflict-marker gate FAILED — commit refused (unresolved merge in staged additions)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- now reads each
# scanned file's STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py, deep_walk_recursion_guard.py's
# own pattern), falling back to the working tree only when a path is not staged at all.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/no_lazy_imports.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: lazy-import gate FAILED — commit refused (CLAUDE.md edict 2026-07-02)." >&2
    echo "Hoist the imports to module top, then commit again." >&2
    exit 1
}

# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): this gate is a layout/tracking
# CENSUS (seen-red/'s on-disk presence cross-checked against `git ls-files` tracking), not a
# content check -- tree-reading the directory listing is correct here (see gates/fixture_census.py's
# own module docstring, point 4); no conversion needed.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/fixture_census.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: fixture census FAILED — commit refused (a gate/seen-red is not intact, ADR-0011/C20)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# fixture_deployment_pin_guard (fixture-scratch-pinning-guard, ledger row 1249): generalizes
# serve_existing_world's own tempdir/repo-disjoint refusal into a mechanical sweep over every
# led-exercising fixture — refuses a fixture that invokes THIS checkout's own operator verbs
# directly (the row-1237-1244/1248 leak class), or that mutates os.environ["PICKUP_DEPLOYMENT"]
# globally instead of pinning per-subprocess. Reads the working tree (same family as
# fixture_census above), scoped to seen-red/, instruments/, kernel/fixtures/.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/fixture_deployment_pin_guard.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: fixture deployment-pin guard FAILED — commit refused (a fixture reaches THIS" >&2
    echo "checkout's own deployment.json instead of a scaffolded scratch copy, or mutates" >&2
    echo "os.environ[\"PICKUP_DEPLOYMENT\"] globally; see gates/fixture_deployment_pin_guard.py's" >&2
    echo "own docstring, fixture-scratch-pinning-guard, ledger row 1249)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# deep_walk_recursion_guard — the single guarded-traversal invariant over
# serving/boundary_service.py (boundary-recursion-net-single-invariant, ledger row 1628). Wired
# 2026-07-23 (review finding against commit d5f809e: the gate existed, seen-red both polarities,
# but was invoked by NOTHING here -- a fourth deep-walk site reintroducing the defect landed
# clean through git commit; the commit message's "mechanically enforces" claim was false as
# delivered until this stanza). This gate was the ORIGINAL specimen of the STAGED-BYTES read
# discipline (git show :./path -- what the commit will actually embed, not whatever the working
# tree happens to hold when the gate runs): stage a violation, restore the tree, and a
# tree-reading gate would pass while the commit still embeds the violation. THIS IS NO LONGER
# THIS GATE'S OWN DIVERGENCE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234, chain-wide census):
# every content-checking gate in this chain now reads staged bytes the same way, via the shared
# gates/_staged_read.py primitive this gate's own read-mode fix was extracted into -- see each
# gate's own comment below for its read-mode disposition. The two gates immediately above
# (no_lazy_imports, fixture_census) are the two genuinely different shapes: no_lazy_imports now
# ALSO reads staged bytes (converted alongside this census); fixture_census reads seen-red/'s
# on-disk PRESENCE cross-checked against `git ls-files` tracking, a layout/tracking census where
# tree-reading the directory listing is the correct query (there is no "staged directory
# listing" to prefer over `os.listdir` -- tracked-or-not is the fact fixture_census needs, and
# `git ls-files` already answers that against the index).
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/deep_walk_recursion_guard.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: deep-walk recursion guard FAILED — commit refused (a RecursionError catch" >&2
    echo "outside _guard_recursion, or a superclass-catch evasion, in serving/boundary_service.py;" >&2
    echo "see gates/deep_walk_recursion_guard.py's own docstring)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# max_lines — ADR-0007's soft file-size threshold, mechanized (design/FABLE-SETUP-TUI-FIELD-
# STRATEGY.md Track 1 item 2): a NEW file over 400 lines in tools/, gates/, hooks/, or engine/ is
# refused outright; a pre-existing offender may only shrink or hold its ratcheted baseline, never
# grow past it. See gates/max_lines.py's own module docstring for the full scope table and
# ratcheting-baseline rationale.
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- line counts now come
# from each file's STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py), tree fallback for unstaged
# paths.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/max_lines.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: max-lines gate FAILED — commit refused (ADR-0007's 400-line ceiling; see" >&2
    echo "gates/max_lines.py's own docstring for the ratcheting baseline and how to read the reason)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# setup_tui_purity_gate — the setup wizard's structural discipline (pure-core spec + typed
# elements: no direct stdin/stdout outside the two renderer files, exemption tables in the
# gate itself). Wired 2026-07-22, the session-boundary batch discharging the wiring queued at
# ledger row 1847 (autoharn1 era) — the gate itself had run green manually on every merge
# since; this makes it mechanical rather than remembered.
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- all three AST
# detectors now scan each file's STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py), tree fallback
# for unstaged paths.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/setup_tui_purity_gate.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: setup-tui purity gate FAILED — commit refused (a wizard module bypasses the typed Ui seam; see gates/setup_tui_purity_gate.py)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# link_integrity — every relative markdown link in tracked *.md must resolve on disk
# (2026-07-11 doc-legibility-indictment commission). Two documented exclusions (judgment/,
# vestigial_documentation/design/ORCH-ARCHITECTURE.md, moved there by the 2026-07-12
# vestigial-doc-sweep) printed in its own output every run — never silent.
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- the linking doc's own
# text is now read from its STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py), tree fallback for
# unstaged paths. The TARGET-existence check (does the linked-to path resolve on disk) is
# primarily a plain filesystem read still, deliberately -- see gates/link_integrity.py's own
# module docstring's READ MODE section. Amended 2026-07-26: a target STAGED FOR DELETION (`git rm
# --cached target.md`, file still physically present) is now ALSO treated as not-existing
# (`staged_deletions()`, closing a real DELETE-direction gap a fresh-context review reproduced --
# a doc's own text being un-re-staged is not the only way this gate could have missed a commit
# that orphans a link). The remaining named residual (a target that is itself staged-but-not-yet-
# on-disk, the ADD direction) stays disclosed, not closed -- see the gate's own docstring for why
# the two directions are treated asymmetrically.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/link_integrity.py" || {
    echo "" >&2
    echo "pre-commit: link-integrity gate FAILED — commit refused (a doc links somewhere that does not exist)." >&2
    exit 1
}

# apparatus_unknown_keys — the shipped apparatus.json default this repo owns must itself carry
# no unrecognized mechanism key (BACKLOG "Configuration-surface survey, adopter's eyes",
# 2026-07-11, gap 1). Gated ONLY when the template is part of this commit (most commits don't
# touch it); report mode (its own default target) is the same file, so this call is redundant
# with the module's own default but explicit here for the blocking case.
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED (partially) -- the
# TARGET apparatus.json is now read from its STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py),
# tree fallback for unstaged paths. NAMED RESIDUAL: the known-mechanism SET this gate checks
# against is derived by filing/apparatus_registry.py scanning hooks/*.py + bootstrap/templates/
# *.tmpl + tools/*.py's own WORKING-TREE source -- shared infrastructure this gate does not own
# and other non-commit-time consumers also read; not converted here (see gates/
# apparatus_unknown_keys.py's own module docstring's READ MODE section).
if git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR | grep -qx "bootstrap/templates/apparatus.json"; then
    "$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/apparatus_unknown_keys.py" "$REPO_ROOT/bootstrap/templates/apparatus.json" || {
        echo "" >&2
        echo "pre-commit: apparatus-unknown-keys gate FAILED — the shipped apparatus.json" >&2
        echo "default carries a mechanism key no hook reads (see gates/apparatus_unknown_keys.py)." >&2
        exit 1
    }
fi

# TOUCHED_MD computed once, shared by doc_shapes and doc-attestation-presence below (both are
# gate-mode, touched-file-scoped checks over the same staged *.md set — one git diff, not two).
TOUCHED_MD=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR -- '*.md')

# doc_shapes — the deterministic zero-context-reader legibility gate (design/ADR-DRAFT-
# documentation-discipline.md Rule 3; BACKLOG "Documentation legibility indictment", 2026-07-11)
# binds ON TOUCH: every changed *.md in this commit must clear FRAGMENT/HANDOFF-POSITIONAL.
# gates/doc_shapes.py's own header names this exact gate-mode invocation shape — built and
# seen-red days before this wiring, never actually invoked from here until the run-10-closure-
# audit commission caught the gap (BACKLOG "Run-10 closure audit (2026-07-11)").
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- gate mode now reads
# each named doc's STAGED bytes by default (gates/_staged_read.py), tree fallback for unstaged
# paths (report mode, the whole-repo sweep -- not invoked from this hook, since it never fails --
# reads the tree unconditionally; this line's claim was stale between 2026-07-25 and its
# 2026-07-26 fix, when the code actually threaded gate mode's `use_tree` into report mode too --
# see gates/doc_shapes.py's own module docstring for the correction, made honest by forcing
# `use_tree=True` in report mode rather than left to rely on the caller passing `--tree`).
if [ -n "$TOUCHED_MD" ]; then
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    "$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/doc_shapes.py" $TOUCHED_MD || {
        echo "" >&2
        echo "pre-commit: doc-shapes gate FAILED — a changed doc has a legibility shape defect" >&2
        echo "(FRAGMENT or HANDOFF-POSITIONAL; see gates/doc_shapes.py's own header)." >&2
        exit 1
    }
fi

# doc-attestation-presence — every touched maintainer-facing *.md must carry a fresh-context
# (A:B:C) attestation record for its exact content (ADR-0017, "The fresh-context audit loop";
# ratified 2026-07-11). Checks PRESENCE+SHAPE only, never the attestation's conclusions — nothing
# here blocks on LLM judgment. This IS gates/doc_attestation_presence.py's own WIRING STANZA,
# applied verbatim (only its target file list generalized to the shared $TOUCHED_MD above).
# READ MODE (gates-staged-vs-tree-blindness, ledger row 1234): CONVERTED -- the content_sha256
# match and the waiver-comment check now read each named doc's STAGED bytes by default
# (gates/_staged_read.py), tree fallback for unstaged paths. The attestation LEDGER file itself
# (attestations/doc-legibility-attestations.jsonl) stays a plain working-tree read -- a record is
# appended by a separate `--record` act, not staged in the same commit as the doc edit it
# attests, so there is no staged/tree gap to close there. Report mode (whole-repo sweep -- not
# invoked from this hook, same as doc_shapes above) was aligned 2026-07-26 to read the tree
# unconditionally too, the same fix doc_shapes.py got, for the same reason (no commit to protect,
# a human debt-sweep wants what's on disk).
if [ -n "$TOUCHED_MD" ]; then
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    "$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/doc_attestation_presence.py" $TOUCHED_MD || {
        echo "" >&2
        echo "pre-commit: doc-attestation-presence FAILED — a changed doc carries no" >&2
        echo "fresh-context attestation record for its current content (ADR-0017)." >&2
        exit 1
    }
fi

# layout_census — DISABLED here (maintainer ruling, 2026-07-09): research repo, census is for
# downstream instances; disabled until further notice. gates/layout_census.py is untouched and
# remains shipped tooling — a downstream template consumer re-enables this block to get the
# ls-legibility guarantee in their own repo. Not removed from gates/, only from this hook's
# enforced set.

# doc-legibility — REPORT-ONLY (see header): runs for visibility, never blocks, pending the
# corpus acronym-sweep (BACKLOG / finding 48). Its exit code is deliberately NOT propagated.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/doc-legibility/check.py" >&2 || \
    echo "pre-commit: doc-legibility reported undefined acronyms (REPORT-ONLY — not blocking; see BACKLOG finding 48)." >&2

# idris-model-freshness — REPORT-ONLY (maintainer promotion of design/Autoharn.idr to
# architecture documentation, 2026-07-15): compares the model's AS-OF line against the actual
# kernel/lineage head and runs idris2 --check. Report-only by its own author's wiring proposal
# (a stale model is true-but-not-actionable for an unrelated committer); upgrade to blocking is
# a deliberate future act, not a default. Exit code deliberately NOT propagated.
"$PY" "$REPO_ROOT/gates/idris_model_freshness.py" >&2 || \
    echo "pre-commit: idris-model-freshness reported the model stale or non-elaborating (REPORT-ONLY — not blocking; ledger item idris-model-freshness-gate)." >&2
